# US-125266 — EPQ Triggers to Reload Tax Lines for DLQ Check After Agency Calendar Dates Change — Detailed Analysis

> Module: Business Tools → Exception Processing Queue → Delinquent Installment Search (DIR).
> Pure SQL-layer fix against `LASTax` (plus read access to `LASTotalTaxSolution` and
> `LASCommon`). No application code (DAL/BLL/UI/Dispatcher) is changed — the two affected
> stored procedures are invoked only by SQL Server Agent job
> `LAS_ExceptionProcessQueue_DataImportNew`, confirmed via full codebase trace to have no
> C#, SSIS, or other stored-procedure caller anywhere in LERETANet or LeretanetCore.

---

## 1. Overview

EPQ's Delinquent Installment Search (DIR) loading process has two confirmed gaps:

**Gap 1 — Eligibility check is a brittle one-shot snapshot.** `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew`
picks the winning ELD date (latest of `ELD0`/`ELDH`/`ELDX` per agency/tax year/installment from
`LASTotalTaxSolution.dbo.lais_PayeeCalendar`) and only flags an installment eligible when
`DATEDIFF(DAY, ELDDate, GETDATE())` is **exactly** equal to the configured `@StartDays` (20).
If that one exact day is missed — job didn't run, data changed later, etc. — the installment is
never picked up again, with no retry. Separately, once a DIR record exists (open or completed),
the existing US-120627 dedup guard in `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` suppresses every
subsequent attempt unconditionally, so a genuine later change to the ELD date never refreshes
the existing record's dates.

**Gap 2 — No current-tax-year validation exists anywhere in the flow.** The eligibility check
has no concept of "is this installment's tax year the current one" — fixing/touching an old
year's calendar data could in principle spawn a brand-new task for a prior year.

**Confirmed via live testing on DEV (2026-11-03):**
- Agency 370020000 (Allegheny) / Loan 15016876: 2026 installment is 187+ days overdue, zero DIR
  record exists for 2026 specifically, despite 5 consecutive prior years (2021-2025) each
  getting a task created and completed normally — a clean, provable regression, not a
  never-worked-at-all case.
- Running the real job (`LAS_ExceptionProcessQueue_DataImportNew`) live on DEV created **zero**
  new exception-queue records of any type (DIR/DMU/TSP) system-wide, despite a backlog of
  ~6,000+ eligible-but-missing installments (Prod) sitting there — because none happened to land
  on exactly day 20 that day. Concrete, live proof of Gap 1's severity, not just static analysis.
- A controlled test (Agency 010370000 / Loan 0000145089: no prior exception-queue record,
  real eligibility config, not cancelled) had its calendar `DueDate` set to exactly 20 days
  overdue; re-running the job correctly created a new DIR record (`ExceptionID 238308`,
  `TaxYear=2026`, `InstallmentDueDate=2026-10-14`, `SLADueDate=2026-12-03`) — confirming the
  underlying creation mechanism itself is sound; only the *exact-match* condition is the problem.

