## 3. Database Changes

**Databases involved:** `LASTax` (all `tbl_ExceptionQueue*` tables, both stored procedures),
`LASTotalTaxSolution` (`lais_PayeeCalendar`, read-only), `LASCommon` (`tbl_Config_Master`,
`lac_AgencyProfile`, read-only).

### SP 1: `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew`

| # | Change | Status |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | ELD tie-break direction — pick the **latest/maximum** of `ELD0`/`ELDH`/`ELDX` | ✅ **No code change needed.** Deployed `ORDER BY v.DueDate DESC` already matches the Lead's final, explicit confirmation ("select the maximum due date"). The SP's own header comment (claims "modified based on the oldest value") and the `US-129258` tSQLt test (`test_ELD_Logic_US129258`, asserts oldest/`ASC`) are both stale/incorrect relative to this confirmed answer — explicitly **out of scope** to fix here (see Dependencies / Section 15). |
| 2 | Eligibility check: exact-match day → catch-up window | 🔲 Planned, not yet coded. Change `DATEDIFF(DAY, w.DueDate, @Getdate) = @StartDays` to a range bounded by the existing, currently-unused `@EndDays` value (already declared and populated from `tbl_Config_Master` in the SP, but never consumed in the current deployed version). |
| 3 | New tax-year validation | ⛔ **Blocked on Question 1.** Once confirmed, add a check so only installments where the computed "current year" for that agency matches the installment's own `CurrentTaxYear` can set `@DLQResearchFlag='1'`. Best candidate formula so far (72.1% system-wide match, not yet finally accepted): `SELECT PayeeID, MAX(CurrentTaxYear) FROM lais_PayeeCalendar WHERE StatusIndicator='C' AND RunCode IN ('ELD0','ELDH','ELDX') GROUP BY PayeeID`. |

### SP 2: `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU`

| # | Change | Status |
|---|---|---|
| 4 | Dedup-guard (US-120627) carve-out | 🔲 Planned. The existing guard is keyed on `LoanID + AgencyID + TaxID + PropertyID + LienSEQ + SystemCode` (open rows only, `UPDLOCK`/`HOLDLOCK`, logged to `tbl_ExceptionQueue_DedupLog` with reason `ADLQ_INGEST_DUPLICATE`) and currently suppresses **any** incoming row unconditionally once a match is found. Add a condition: if the incoming ELD-derived due date genuinely differs from the existing open row's stored value, proceed to UPDATE instead of suppressing — scoped to `SystemCode='DIR'` only, so DMU/TSP behavior is untouched. |
| 5 | Field-refresh scope on update | 🔲 Planned. **Open** items: refresh `InstallmentDueDate`, `SLADueDate`, and the Load Date (`InsertedDate`, shown as "Date Added" on screen). **Completed** items: refresh `InstallmentDueDate` (ELD) only — `SLADueDate`/Load Date left untouched (per the PO's original worked example; this is the user's own working decision, not a separately re-confirmed PO answer). |
| 6 | Audit note | 🔲 Planned. Add a new call to `Usp_exceptionqueue_history_ins` with comment text flagging "updated due to ELD recalculation" whenever change #4/#5 actually updates an existing record. No change to `Usp_exceptionqueue_history_ins` itself. |

