## 13. Edge Cases

| Case | Handling |
|---|---|
| Contract-cancelled loans (`lat_ContractMasterKey.LCR_CANCEL_CODE='C'`) | Unaffected by this change — already routed through the separate `usp_ExceptionQueue_AutoCompleted_Upd` auto-complete path, not the eligibility/dedup logic being modified here. |
| Agencies/loans with multiple liens across many tax years (e.g., Allegheny has 6 distinct `TaxID`s just for 2025, with 2 of those same `TaxID`s also appearing under 2024) | Confirmed `TaxID` alone does **not** reliably distinguish tax years for the same loan — the "already has a DIR record" check must be scoped through `tbl_ExceptionQueue_Tax_Info.TaxYear`/`InstallmentNo`, not `TaxID` alone, or old years' completed records can mask a genuinely missing current year. This is already how the discovery/report queries built during analysis are scoped; the planned SP changes must follow the same pattern. |
| Two loans found during live DEV testing that passed every known eligibility gate (real config, not cancelled, no existing record, `Late_Rels<>'U'`) yet were **not** processed by a live job run (Agency 120310000 Installment 2/2025; Agency 330090000, Loan 0000068049) | **Unresolved.** Root cause not found during analysis — would require reading `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` with debug instrumentation, or re-testing after Gap 1's fix is in place (the fix may incidentally resolve or further isolate this). Flagged as a known loose end, not confirmed to be caused by either Gap. |

