## 14. Assumptions

- "Current tax year" validation applies **going forward only** — no retroactive correction of
  existing EPQ records (PO-confirmed).
- The system should **update** an existing record rather than create a duplicate when the ELD
  value changes (PO-confirmed).
- New, Open, and Follow-Up states are treated identically for this story's purposes (PO-confirmed).
- No backfill/creation of DIR records for installments already found missing by the discovery
  report (including the ~6,000+ found on Prod) — report/visibility only (user-confirmed; reads
  consistently with the PO's forward-only answer above, though never asked as a separately
  worded question).
- Catch-up window upper bound reuses the existing `@EndDays` config value (user-confirmed).
- Completed items refresh only the ELD date on update, not SLA/Load Date (user's own working
  decision — hedged as "I think," not independently re-confirmed with the PO).
- Fixing `US-129258`'s backwards tSQLt test is explicitly **out of scope** for this ticket
  (user-confirmed) — needs its own separate follow-up ticket.

